	  <div class="acc-job-post">
        <div class="job-details" data-attribute="jp-3">
          <div class="job-role">
            <h3>Software Developer</h3>
            <span>Posted on 01-Mar-2024</span>
          </div>
          <div class="job-location">
            <span
              >BlueBinaries Engineering and Solutions Inc., Troy, MI</span
            >
            <img src="https://www.bluebinaries.com/wp-content/themes/bluebinaries/assets/images/down-arrow.png" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="job-requirements"  id="jp-3">
            <p><b>Responsibilities & Key Deliverables:</b></p>
			                <p><b>1. CAN DEVELOPMENT</b><p>

            <ul>
			<li>Lead the development and integration of Controller Area Network (CAN) Communication protocol for various automotive applications e.g BMS, CCM, Infotainment system.</li>
			<li>Design and Implement CAN network configurations, including message scheduling and Bus arbitration.</li>
			<li>Perform CAN network diagnostics, fault handling and ensure robust communication between ECUs.</li>
			</ul>
			<p><b>2. Basic Software AUTOSAR</b></p>
			<ul>
			<li>Develop and maintain AUTOSAR based basic software modules ensuring, compliance with AUTOSAR standards and guidelines.</li>
			<li>Configure and integrate AUTOSAR BSW stack components, including COM, PDU Router, CanIf, CAN and Diagnostic Event Manager (DEM).</li>
			<li>Collaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure seamless integration of AUTOSAR software components into the overall vehicle architecture.</li>
			</ul>
			<p><b>3. Network Management</b></p>
			<ul>
			<li>Design and implement network management strategies for automotive systems, ensuring optimal network performance and reliability.</li>
			<li>Configure and manage network management protocols, including Startup, Shutdown and Sleep/wake- Up sequences.</li>
			<li>Perform Network performance analysis and optimization to meet stringent automotive industry standards.</li>
			<li>Handle Partial Networking to ensure power saving in the network.</li>
			</ul>
			<p><b>4. Requirement Writing</b></p>
			<ul>
			<li>Develop detailed software requirements for Level 3 and Level 4 automotive software components, ensuring clarity, completeness and traceability.</li>
			<li>Collaborate with system engineers and stakeholders to capture and refine requirements, ensuring alignment with overall system architecture and design.</li>
			<li>Use Doors Next Gen to maintain and track requirements changes and their impact on software development lifecycles.</li>
			</ul>
			<p><b>5. Functional Safety (ISO 26262)</b></p>
			<ul>
			<li>Support functional safety activities in accordance with ISO 26262 standards including hazard analysis and risk assessment (HARA).</li>
			<li>Assist in the development of safety requirements and safety cases for automotive software components.</li>
			</ul>
			<p><b>6. Agile Methodology</b></p>
			<ul>
			<li>Actively participate in Agile development processes, including sprint planning, daily stand-ups, and retrospectives.</li>
			<li>Collaborate in a cross-functional agile team to deliver quality software within define sprint cycle.</li>
			<li>Adapt and respond to changes in project scope and priorities in an Agile environment, ensuring timely delivery of project milestones.</li>
			</ul>
			<p><b>7. V-Model Development </b></p>
			<ul>
			<li>Apply V-Model development processes to ensure comprehensive testing and validation at each stage of the software development lifecycle.</li>
			<li>Develop and execute test cases and validation plans corresponding to each phase of the V-Model, ensuring through verification and validation of software components.</li>
			<li>Document and trace software requirements and test results, ensuring compliance with the V-Model framework and industry standards.</li>
			</ul>
			<p><b>8. Project Leadership and Collaboration</b></p>
			<ul>
			<li>Mentor junior engineers, providing technical guidance and ensuring adherence to best practices and industry standards.</li>
			<li>Coordinate with cross-functional teams, including hardware, system, and validation engineers, to ensure successful project execution.</li>
			<li>Participate in project planning, status meetings, and technical reviews, contributing to project risk management and mitigation strategies.</li>
			</ul>
			<p><b>9. Unit Testing and Development</b></p>
			<ul>
			<li>Develop and execute unit tests for CAN bus software components, ensuring functionality and performance with respect to design specifications.</li>
			<li>Debugging and root cause analysis of software problems using Trace 32.</li>
			<li>Validation of CAN network communication to ensure software robustness.</li>
			<li>Maintain documentation of test results and debugging activities.</li>
			</ul>
			<p><b>10. Documentation and reporting</b></p>
			<ul>
			<li>Prepare and maintain comprehensive documentation for all phases of software development, including design specifications, test plans and user manuals.</li>
			<li>Generate and present technical reports and progress updates to stakeholders and management.</li>
			<li>Ensure compliance with industry standards, company policies, and regulatory requirements throughout the software development process.</li>
			</ul>

            <!--<a class="commonbtn2" href="#" target="_blank">Click Here To Apply</a>-->
        </div>
      </div>
	  
